A blind leaf split allocates its two halves before it reads the separator
key from the data file, so a read error there (EIO) leaks both leaves.
Reverts #652's fix.
Disable: power,sigkill
Expected: NOT caught: the mutation check runs the release worker without
LeakSanitizer, and a leaked node changes no result the rig compares. The
nightly ASan isolation chaos run found it (run 40269378565); the unit test
below catches it.
Guarded-by: "blind tree: a read that fails during a write leaks no node"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm b/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
index 16ed503..f5fd1c0 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/blind_btree.cppm
@@ -716,15 +716,6 @@ private:
       m = 1;
     m = std::clamp<std::uint32_t>(m, 1, total - 1);
 
-    // The separator read can throw (a read error) and so can its copy: both
-    // run before the leaves are allocated, so a failure leaks neither.
-    const auto cut = std::size_t{meta[m] >> 12 >> kPosShift} + 1;
-    const Bytes first_right =
-        m == p.idx ? key : res.key_at(L::ref_of(loc[m]));
-    assert(cut <= first_right.size());
-    sep_.assign(first_right.begin(),
-                first_right.begin() + static_cast<std::ptrdiff_t>(cut));
-
     auto *left = L::allocate(tag_);
     L::copy(L::arrays(left), 0, tmp, 0, m);
     left->count = m;
@@ -738,6 +729,13 @@ private:
       left->last_pos = static_cast<std::uint16_t>(p.idx);
     else
       right->last_pos = static_cast<std::uint16_t>(p.idx - m);
+
+    const auto cut = std::size_t{meta[m] >> 12 >> kPosShift} + 1;
+    const Bytes first_right =
+        m == p.idx ? key : res.key_at(L::ref_of(loc[m]));
+    assert(cut <= first_right.size());
+    sep_.assign(first_right.begin(),
+                first_right.begin() + static_cast<std::ptrdiff_t>(cut));
     discard(leaf);
     return {left, right, true, true};
   }
